{
  "_doc": "One row per case of the store-path check, read by the approval hook's test, the executor's test and their parity test. `expected` is the rule's outcome: `ask` (the hook asks and stamps; the executor runs only on that stamp), `deny` (the hook denies and files no stamp; the executor refuses, and when `deny_reason` is `store_path` it refuses even with a stamp), `defer` (the hook makes no decision because the writes posture refuses; the executor refuses: nothing was stamped), `unchanged` (no marker: the hook decides as it would for neutral code, and the executor's store-path check does not apply). `deny_reason` names which deny the hook gives. `execute_file` rows carry the file's text in `code`; the hook sees only a path, so only the executor is asserted for them.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "relative-dir-in-string-always-readonly",
      "tool": "execute",
      "code": "data = open('_agent_data/control_target/notes.txt').read()\n",
      "policy": "always", "enabled": true, "execution_mode": "readonly",
      "dispatch": false, "switch": "on", "expected": "ask"
    },
    {
      "id": "absolute-record-selective-readonly",
      "tool": "execute",
      "code": "from pathlib import Path\nprint(Path('/srv/osprey/state/control_context.json').read_text())\n",
      "policy": "selective", "enabled": true, "execution_mode": "readonly",
      "dispatch": false, "switch": "on", "expected": "ask"
    },
    {
      "id": "marker-in-comment-selective-readonly",
      "tool": "execute",
      "code": "x = 1  # the switch lives in control_target\nprint(x)\n",
      "policy": "selective", "enabled": true, "execution_mode": "readonly",
      "dispatch": false, "switch": "on", "expected": "ask"
    },
    {
      "id": "record-in-string-selective-readwrite",
